# rena0-powered-shot — F1-3 fixture, P2-7 charge family (the powered air tap)
#
# Source: Rena+0's air-tap body (FUN_0043ffc0.c:1968-2020) emits its shot at frame 13 and picks
# the bullet row from the held-aim pair `+0x845`/`+0x212` — row 7 when both are set, row 1
# otherwise (:2009-2014, :1961-1965). That path performs NO subtraction of the shot gauge.
# Q19 withdrew the earlier claim that FUN_00508a60's −500 was this spend: there it is a
# directional air-dash cancel out of state 402 into state 30, in another combo's selector.
#
# So this fixture pins the powered launch and its cost: the shot that leaves the fighter is
# bullet row 7 (the ordinary ground tap is row 0, rena0-tap-shot.fixture), and `charge_gauge`
# is unchanged by the launch itself — it reads the 1000 cap throughout. The scripted jump
# costs nothing to launch (no jump body charges one); its launch tick carries the row-40
# refill (+40, clamped here), and the powered 402 emission subtracts nothing.
#
# `hyper oyashiro` fills the gauge, selects Oyashiro and arms the aim selection; the SPECIAL
# press at tick 0 is the real activation edge (fighter.cpp:843).
combo 0 0
seed 5489
spawn 0 0 0 0
spawn 1 0 0 300
collision open-field
hyper oyashiro
input 0 SPECIAL
input 1 -
input 4 JUMP
input 5 -
input 10 SHOOT
input 11 -
expect 24 charge_gauge 1000
expect 25 shot_bullet_row 7
expect 25 charge_gauge 1000
expect 40 charge_gauge 1000
